     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ancient Marathi Ritual &quot;Gondhal&quot; Takes Center Stage as India's Oscar Entry</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Gondhal</span> <span>#Marathi Cinema</span> <span>#Oscars</span> <span>#Indian Culture</span></div>
       <p>A centuries-old Marathi folk ritual, Gondhal, has garnered international attention as the inspiration behind India's official entry to the 99th Academy Awards. On September 18, 2026, the film &quot;Gondhal&quot; was unanimously selected for the Best International Feature Film category, bringing a global spotlight to a tradition long performed quietly in family courtyards.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/ancient-marathi-ritual-gondhal-takes-center-stage-as-indias-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gondhal is one of Maharashtra's oldest living folk art forms, where hereditary performers, called Gondhalis, sing mythological stories and express gratitude to family deities. Dressed in vivid colors and often tossing lit torches, they perform to the rhythm of sambal drums, tal cymbals, and chipli clappers, while women join in a swirling dance. This ritual, passed down through generations, is a binding family custom after significant life events like weddings or overcoming illnesses.</p><p>Directed by Santosh Davakhar, the film &quot;Gondhal&quot; weaves a story around this tradition, featuring a 25-minute single continuous shot—a notable technical achievement that earned it the Best Director award at the 56th International Film Festival of India. Released in Indian cinemas on November 14, 2025, with music by Ilaiyaraaja, the film was praised by the Film Federation of India jury for its technical execution and fusion of style with substance. This selection marks a historic honor for Marathi cinema and Maharashtra's rich folk traditions.</p><p>Why it matters: The film's Oscar entry elevates a significant cultural heritage to a global platform, ensuring broader recognition and appreciation for Maharashtra's vibrant folk traditions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a precise and factual summary of the provided text regarding the film Gondhal.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/culture/gondhal-marathi-film-india-oscar-entry-ritual-12567686" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
