     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-09-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>China's Yu Zidi, 13, Wins Third Gold With Latest Asian Games Record</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Swimming</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#Yu Zidi</span> <span>#Sports</span></div>
       <p>Chinese swimmer Yu Zidi, a prodigious talent at just 13 years old, has achieved a remarkable milestone at the Asian Games. The young athlete secured her third gold medal on Wednesday, capping a dominant performance in the 400m individual medley event.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/chinas-yu-zidi-13-wins-third-gold-with-latest-asian-games-re.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This latest victory not only cemented her status as a rising star but also saw her establish a new Asian Games record. Her consistent excellence and ability to break records at such a young age have drawn considerable attention within the international swimming community.</p><p>Yu Zidi's hat-trick of gold medals underscores China's strong presence in competitive swimming and highlights the depth of talent emerging from its youth sports programs. Her success in the 400m individual medley, a demanding event that tests versatility across multiple strokes, demonstrates her comprehensive skill set and rigorous training regimen.</p><p>The achievement marks a significant moment in the ongoing Asian Games, showcasing individual brilliance and national sporting prowess. For a 13-year-old to dominate in such a high-stakes international competition suggests a promising future in the sport. Her ability to deliver under pressure and consistently outpace competitors points to an athlete with exceptional potential for future global events.</p><p>What to watch: Yu Zidi's continued development and performance in upcoming international competitions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided summary, adding minor, reasonable editorial context about the athlete's potential.</p>
