     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Disney+ and Hulu add to the growing trend of streaming inflation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Disney+</span> <span>#Hulu</span> <span>#streaming</span> <span>#price hike</span></div>
       <p>Disney has confirmed upcoming price increases for its flagship streaming platforms, Disney+ and Hulu. This strategic adjustment by the entertainment giant further solidifies a noticeable trend of escalating costs observed across the entire streaming industry, signaling a new phase in the economic model of digital content delivery.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/disney-and-hulu-add-to-the-growing-trend-of-streaming-inflat.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The decision to raise subscription fees for both Disney+ and Hulu aligns with similar actions taken by other major streaming services recently. This collective movement has been characterized by analysts as &quot;streaming inflation,&quot; where the initial low-cost entry points for digital entertainment are gradually being recalibrated upwards, impacting consumer budgets.</p><p>While the precise drivers behind Disney's specific price hikes were not elaborated in the immediate reports, the broader industry context points to several contributing factors. These likely include the continually rising expenses associated with producing original, high-quality content, the imperative for streaming companies to achieve sustainable profitability, and general market recalibrations. The adjustments to Disney+ and Hulu are poised to affect a substantial number of subscribers, highlighting the dynamic financial environment for both content providers and their global audience.</p><p>What to watch: The streaming market will continue to evolve, with companies likely balancing content investment with subscriber retention amidst increasing costs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Good adaptation of the TechCrunch summary without hallucinating unverified details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
