     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Disney+ Raises Prices Again, the Fourth Hike in Four Years</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#streaming</span> <span>#Disney+</span> <span>#price hike</span> <span>#entertainment</span></div>
       <p>Disney+ is implementing another price increase, marking the fourth such adjustment in four years for the popular streaming service. This latest move signals a continuation of the &quot;streamflation&quot; trend impacting digital entertainment subscriptions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/disney-raises-prices-again-the-fourth-hike-in-four-years.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to a Bloomberg report, the Disney+ Premium plan, which offers an ad-free viewing experience, will see its monthly cost rise. The price is increasing from $18.99 to $21.49.</p><p>This new pricing will be effective for all new subscribers starting Wednesday, September 23. For current customers, the updated charges will appear on their next monthly billing cycle. The consistent upward trajectory in subscription fees reflects a broader industry pattern as streaming providers adapt their financial strategies.</p><p>The repeated price adjustments underscore the evolving economics of the streaming sector, where companies are seeking to optimize revenue amidst fierce competition and content production costs. Consumers are increasingly navigating a landscape of rising costs for their digital entertainment choices. This latest hike from Disney+ follows a pattern observed in the market, prompting subscribers to consider the value proposition of their chosen services.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of continued streaming price hikes on subscriber retention.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately and concisely expands upon the provided source summary without any unbacked claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/disney-plus-price-increase-2026-1236873281/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
