     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>FSSAI Ex-Chief Proposes Phased Food Warning Rollout</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#FSSAI</span> <span>#Food Safety</span> <span>#Supreme Court</span> <span>#Pawan Kumar Agarwal</span></div>
       <p>Former Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) chief Pawan Kumar Agarwal has urged the Supreme Court to consider a phased rollout of front-of-pack food warnings. He argued that the currently proposed nutrient thresholds are too broad, potentially placing warning labels on more than 94% of packaged foods. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/fssai-ex-chief-proposes-phased-food-warning-rollout.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Agarwal warned that such a high prevalence of labels could dilute their impact, making it difficult for consumers to distinguish between healthier and less healthy options. To address this, his foundation suggested a more gradual approach. </p><p>The proposal involves setting interim thresholds first, followed by stricter limits over a period of three to five years. This phased strategy aims to ensure that the warning labels remain meaningful and effective in guiding consumer choices. </p><p>Under the suggested timeline, mandatory labelling would be proposed to start from July 1, 2027. This allows for a transition period where the industry can adapt to the new regulations while the criteria are tightened. </p><p>Agarwal’s intervention highlights the ongoing debate over how to implement effective food safety regulations without overwhelming consumers or the market. </p><p>What to watch: The Supreme Court’s ruling on the implementation timeline for front-of-pack food warnings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/policy/94-of-packaged-foods-may-face-warnings-under-nutrient-limits-fssai-ex-chief-pawan-kumar-agarwal-urges-sc-for-phased-food-warning-rollout/134424130" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
