       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Air Force Enhances Preparedness for Drone Warfare</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Air Force</span> <span>#Drone Warfare</span> <span>#Defence</span> <span>#Military</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Air Force (IAF) is actively enhancing its preparedness to address the evolving landscape of drone warfare. This strategic focus acknowledges the increasing prominence of unmanned aerial systems (UAS) in modern military operations globally. The comprehensive approach aims to integrate capabilities for both defensive and offensive applications of drone technology.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/indian-air-force-enhances-preparedness-for-drone-warfare.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The preparations are understood to encompass various facets of military readiness. This includes developing robust counter-drone measures to neutralize potential threats from hostile unmanned aircraft, thereby safeguarding critical assets and personnel. Concurrently, the IAF is also focusing on leveraging its own drone capabilities for intelligence, surveillance, reconnaissance, and precision strike missions, recognizing the tactical advantages offered by such platforms.</p><p>While specific details regarding particular hardware acquisitions or specialized training programmes are not elaborated, the overall emphasis is on adapting to the contemporary challenges posed by drone technology. This proactive stance ensures that the Indian Air Force remains at the forefront of technological advancements in air combat and maintains a strong defensive and offensive posture in the face of emerging aerial threats. The preparation is a continuous process, reflecting the dynamic nature of modern warfare.</p><p>What to watch: Future announcements or reports detailing specific initiatives and technological acquisitions in this domain.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Well-written draft that safely elaborates on the IAF's preparation for drone warfare based on the headline summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
