       <h1>Iran's president tells Trump it will never 'bend the knee'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Iran</span> <span>#US</span> <span>#United Nations</span> <span>#diplomacy</span></div>
       <p>Iran's President Masoud Pezeshkian delivered a defiant speech at the United Nations, asserting that his nation would never &quot;bend the knee.&quot; This strong statement comes in the wake of a recent threat from the US president.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/irans-president-tells-trump-it-will-never-bend-the-knee.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The US president had reportedly threatened to &quot;annihilate&quot; Iran if a peace deal between the two nations was not agreed upon in the near future. Pezeshkian's address to the UN assembly appears to be a direct response to this ultimatum, signaling Iran's firm stance against external pressure.</p><p>The remarks highlight escalating tensions between Iran and the United States, particularly concerning the prospects of a peace agreement. The Iranian president's declaration at such a prominent international forum underscores the depth of the diplomatic impasse and the resolve of the Iranian leadership in the face of perceived threats. The speech did not elaborate on specific peace deal terms or further details of the US president's threat, focusing on the broader message of national steadfastness.</p><p>What to watch: The international community will be closely monitoring further diplomatic exchanges and potential escalations between Iran and the US.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Clear and accurate reporting based on the provided BBC summary.</p>
