     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jay Meena Targets India's First Soft Tennis Medal</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Jay Meena</span> <span>#Soft Tennis</span> <span>#Asian Games 2026</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Indian soft tennis player Jay Meena has expressed confidence in securing India’s first-ever medal in the sport at the Asian Games. His assurance comes after he advanced to the men’s singles semi-finals at the Aichi-Nagoya 2026 edition. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/jay-meena-targets-indias-first-soft-tennis-medal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Meena’s progression to the semi-finals marks a significant milestone for Indian soft tennis on the international stage. The sport, while gaining traction, has yet to yield a medal for India in this premier multi-sport event. </p><p>By reaching the final four, Meena has positioned himself to compete for a place on the podium. His performance in the upcoming semi-final match will determine whether he advances to the final and potentially claims history for the country. </p><p>The Aichi-Nagoya 2026 Asian Games provide a crucial platform for Meena to showcase his skills against top competitors from across Asia. His journey to the semi-finals demonstrates his growing competitiveness in the global soft tennis circuit. </p><p>As the tournament progresses, attention turns to the semi-final clash where Meena will face a determined opponent. A win would secure his spot in the final and keep the dream of a historic medal alive. </p><p>What to watch: Jay Meena’s performance in the men’s singles semi-final match at the Aichi-Nagoya 2026 Asian Games.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
