       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jeffrey Katzenberg Says Hollywood Must Accept AI as a Tool: It ‘Is Not Going Away’</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Jeffrey Katzenberg</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Hollywood</span> <span>#entertainment industry</span></div>
       <p>Jeffrey Katzenberg, the renowned Hollywood producer and executive, has issued a clear message to the entertainment industry: accept artificial intelligence (AI) as an indispensable tool for future relevance. This perspective was detailed in a substantial 2,377-word essay that Katzenberg posted to the social media platform X on Wednesday.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/jeffrey-katzenberg-says-hollywood-must-accept-ai-as-a-tool-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Throughout his career, Katzenberg has witnessed and adapted to numerous technological transformations within Hollywood. In his recent essay, he leveraged this extensive history to frame the current debate surrounding AI. He argued that the entertainment sector has a precedent for integrating new technologies, suggesting that AI is merely the latest in a long line of innovations that demand acceptance.</p><p>Katzenberg's central plea to his creative colleagues is to recognize AI's role as a tool. He positioned AI not as an existential threat, but as an instrument comparable to other technological shifts that have previously reshaped the industry. His message is a call for creatives to acknowledge the permanence of AI and to integrate it into their workflows to ensure Hollywood's continued innovation and impact.</p><p>What to watch: Industry leaders and creative professionals will likely continue to debate and explore the practical applications and ethical considerations of AI integration in entertainment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the details from the Variety summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/biz/news/jeffrey-katzenberg-hollywood-must-accept-not-going-away-1236873535/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
