     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>LSR Students Protest For Safety, Desolate Back Lane Exposes Lack Of CCTVs And Harassment</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#student protest</span> <span>#campus safety</span> <span>#LSR College</span> <span>#national news</span></div>
       <p>Students at Lady Shri Ram College (LSR) have launched protests, demanding enhanced safety measures following concerns over a desolate back lane adjacent to the campus. The demonstrations aim to highlight critical security deficiencies that students believe expose them to significant risks.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/lsr-students-protest-for-safety-desolate-back-lane-exposes-l.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The core issues raised by the protesting students revolve around a pronounced lack of Closed-Circuit Television (CCTV) cameras in the identified back lane. This absence of surveillance is reportedly contributing to an environment where instances of harassment have occurred. The students contend that the unmonitored nature of this area makes it a vulnerable spot, compromising their personal safety.</p><p>Their collective action underscores a call for immediate intervention from both college administration and relevant local authorities. Students are pressing for the swift installation of CCTV cameras and other essential security infrastructure to transform the high-risk lane into a safer passage. The protests represent a unified stand against perceived negligence in ensuring a secure campus perimeter.</p><p>This student-led movement at LSR College brings to the fore wider discussions about campus security protocols and the responsibility of institutions to safeguard their students, particularly in surrounding public spaces. The ongoing demonstrations reflect the students' determination to secure a safer academic and residential environment, free from the threats of harassment and insecurity in crucial transit areas.</p><p>What to watch: Official responses and proposed solutions to the LSR students' safety concerns.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the essence of the LSR student protests for safety and CCTV installation.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/lsr-students-protest-for-safety-desolate-back-lane-exposes-lack-of-cctvs-and-harassment-ytvd-3001444-2026-09-23?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
