       <h1>Nani Addresses 'A' Rating for 'The Paradise' at Mumbai Press Meet</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#The Paradise</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Film Certification</span> <span>#Nani</span></div>
       <p>The cast of the upcoming film 'The Paradise', including Nani, Sonali Kulkarni, Raghav Juyal, and Kayadu Lohar, recently convened for a press meet in Mumbai. A significant point of discussion at the event revolved around the film's certification status.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/nani-addresses-a-rating-for-the-paradise-at-mumbai-press-mee.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>It was revealed on September 21 that 'The Paradise', an action entertainer, has been granted an 'A' certificate by the Central Board of Film Certification (CBFC). This rating typically signifies content suitable only for adults.</p><p>During the press interaction, Nani was directly questioned about the 'A' rating. He took the opportunity to explain the rationale behind the certification, asserting that the film does not feature &quot;violence for the sake of violence.&quot; Nani further emphasized that despite the rating, audiences could watch the film &quot;with your families, parents,&quot; suggesting that the content, while mature, is not gratuitously offensive.</p><p>What to watch: The audience reception to 'The Paradise' and its 'A' rating upon release.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the press meet details and the actor's comments.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/the-paradise-mumbai-press-meet-nani-breaks-silence-on-receiving-a-rating-our-film-doesnt-have-violence-for-the-sake-of-violenceyou-can-watch-this-film-wi/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
