     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-09-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NASA’s Hubble Space Telescope Achieves 200,000 Orbits Milestone</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NASA</span> <span>#Hubble</span> <span>#Space Telescope</span> <span>#Astronomy</span></div>
       <p>NASA’s venerable Hubble Space Telescope has reached a significant operational milestone, completing its 200,000th orbit around Earth on September 19. This achievement further solidifies Hubble's legacy as a pivotal observatory that continues to reshape humanity's understanding of the cosmos.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/nasas-hubble-space-telescope-achieves-200000-orbits-mileston.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Over its remarkable 36-year lifetime, the Hubble Space Telescope has traversed an immense distance, traveling more than 5 billion miles in its journey around our planet. This extensive operational period has enabled the observatory to conduct an extraordinary volume of scientific work, exceeding 1.7 million total observations.</p><p>The 200,000th orbit underscores the enduring capability and scientific productivity of the telescope, which has consistently delivered groundbreaking data and stunning imagery since its deployment. An observation was completed on the very day of this orbital milestone, continuing its mission to explore distant galaxies, stars, and other celestial phenomena.</p><p>Hubble’s contributions have been instrumental in numerous astronomical discoveries, from measuring the expansion rate of the universe to capturing the birth and death of stars, continually pushing the boundaries of astrophysical research.</p><p>What to watch: Future scientific observations and data releases from the ongoing Hubble mission.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Consistent with source summary; no unbacked statements.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/missions/hubble/nasas-hubble-seeks-lensed-supernova-marks-200000-orbits/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
