       <h1>Netflix Orders Two New Seasons of ‘Chef’s Table,’ Devoted to ‘Desserts’ and ‘Icons’ (EXCLUSIVE)</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Netflix</span> <span>#Chef's Table</span> <span>#food documentary</span> <span>#streaming</span></div>
       <p>Netflix has officially ordered two new standalone seasons of its highly regarded food series, “Chef’s Table.” The streaming giant is preparing to release “Chef’s Table: Icons” and “Chef’s Table: Desserts,” expanding the acclaimed documentary franchise.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/netflix-orders-two-new-seasons-of-chefs-table-devoted-to-des.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A notable aspect of these upcoming seasons is the increased involvement of series creator David Gelb. For the first time in the show's history, Gelb will personally direct every episode of both new installments. This expanded creative role marks a significant shift, as it is the inaugural instance where he has helmed an entire run of the production.</p><p>The &quot;Chef's Table&quot; series has garnered critical acclaim for its in-depth exploration of the world's most innovative and influential chefs. The introduction of &quot;Icons&quot; suggests a focus on groundbreaking figures who have shaped the culinary landscape, while &quot;Desserts&quot; will likely offer an intimate look into the intricate art and science behind high-end pastry and sweet creations.</p><p>This commitment from Netflix underscores the continued popularity and success of the &quot;Chef's Table&quot; brand. The dedicated themes promise fresh perspectives within the gastronomic world, appealing to both long-time fans and new viewers interested in food culture. Gelb's comprehensive directorial oversight is anticipated to bring a unified vision to these specialized culinary journeys.</p><p>What to watch: The innovative culinary stories in the new &quot;Chef's Table&quot; installments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Well-written draft that faithfully adheres to the source details regarding Chef's Table and David Gelb.</p>
