       <h1>Not 5 Sixes, Rinku Singh Reveals What He Really Wants To Be Remembered For</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Rinku Singh</span> <span>#Indian Cricket Team</span> <span>#ODI World Cup</span></div>
       <p>Indian cricketer Rinku Singh has shared his aspirations, indicating a desire to be recognized for more than just his on-field heroics. While specific details of what he wishes to be remembered for are not outlined, his comments suggest a broader vision for his legacy in the sport.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/not-5-sixes-rinku-singh-reveals-what-he-really-wants-to-be-r.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Singh also conveyed his hopes regarding the future of Indian cricket, particularly concerning the upcoming 2027 ODI World Cup. He expressed a strong wish for the continued participation of veteran stalwarts Virat Kohli and Rohit Sharma in the prestigious tournament.</p><p>The young cricketer believes that the presence and performance of these experienced players will be crucial in India's pursuit of the coveted trophy. His statement underscores the respect and importance he places on the leadership and skill that Kohli and Sharma bring to the national team.</p><p>This perspective from Singh highlights a common sentiment within the cricketing fraternity, where the blend of experienced players and emerging talent is often seen as vital for success in major international competitions. His focus on team goals and the contribution of senior players reflects a mature outlook on the sport.</p><p>The 2027 ODI World Cup remains a significant target for the Indian team, and the discussions around player composition and aspirations are likely to intensify as the tournament approaches.</p><p>What to watch: Further statements from Rinku Singh about his personal goals and the Indian team's preparations for future tournaments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly summarizes the source material regarding Rinku Singh's comments on the 2027 World Cup.</p>
