      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/health">health</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · BBC Health · 2026-09-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Open wounds and eyes that can't close - women warn about cheap bleph eyelid surgery</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health</span> <span>#Cosmetic Surgery</span> <span>#Medical Tourism</span> <span>#Eyelid Surgery</span></div>
       <p>Women who have undergone inexpensive blepharoplasty, or eyelid surgery, are increasingly raising alarms about severe post-operative complications. Reports include distressing issues such as open wounds and the inability to fully close their eyes, highlighting significant concerns with certain procedures.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/open-wounds-and-eyes-that-cant-close-women-warn-about-cheap-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Medical professionals are observing a concerning trend, noting that a growing number of patients are presenting with problems stemming from treatments received abroad. This phenomenon points to potential risks associated with seeking cosmetic surgeries in foreign clinics, particularly when cost is the primary driving factor.</p><p>The complications described, such as persistent open wounds, suggest inadequate surgical techniques, poor hygiene standards, or insufficient post-operative care. The inability to close eyelids properly can lead to severe dry eye, corneal damage, and other long-term vision issues, drastically impacting patients' quality of life.</p><p>Doctors are urging caution for individuals considering cosmetic procedures overseas, emphasizing the importance of thorough research into clinics, surgeons' qualifications, and the standards of care. The low cost of some treatments may mask significant risks that can result in serious health consequences and the need for corrective surgeries, which can be both complex and expensive.</p><p>What to watch: The ongoing efforts by medical bodies to regulate and inform patients about medical tourism risks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively expands on the provided summary while maintaining accuracy regarding the risks of medical tourism.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
