     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Raichandani's 110* helps India U-19 whitewash Australia U-19 3-0</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India U-19</span> <span>#Australia U-19</span> <span>#Whitewash</span></div>
       <p>India U-19 clinched a dominant 3-0 series whitewash against Australia U-19, with Raichandani’s magnificent unbeaten 110-run knock proving instrumental in sealing the final victory. This comprehensive performance underscored the Indian side's exceptional talent and depth, allowing them to sweep the series in emphatic fashion.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/raichandanis-110-helps-india-u-19-whitewash-australia-u-19-3.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the decisive encounter, India U-19 successfully chased down a challenging target. Earlier, the Australian U-19 team was bowled out for 254. This total, while respectable, ultimately proved insufficient against a resolute Indian batting lineup. The foundation for India's chase was laid by a stellar bowling effort, with Manal Chauhan and Mohit Ulva leading the attack. Both bowlers were in superb form, each bagging three crucial wickets to effectively dismantle the Australian batting order and restrict their scoring. Their disciplined spells created the perfect platform for the batsmen to secure the win.</p><p>Raichandani's century was a display of controlled aggression and maturity, guiding his team through the chase with remarkable ease. His individual brilliance, combined with the collective team effort, ensured India U-19 maintained their unbeaten run throughout the series. This dominant whitewash not only highlights the promising future of Indian cricket but also reflects the effectiveness of their youth development programs.</p><p>What to watch: The continued rise of these young talents in future international competitions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source information provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1555484.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
