     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-09-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Record savings on medical expenses under Ayushman Bharat: PM Modi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ayushman Bharat</span> <span>#Modi</span> <span>#Healthcare</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi has announced that the Ayushman Bharat scheme has facilitated record savings on medical expenses for its beneficiaries across the nation. The Prime Minister conveyed this significant achievement in a post on X, marking a notable milestone for the flagship public health initiative.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/record-savings-on-medical-expenses-under-ayushman-bharat-pm-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In his statement, Modi reflected on the foundational principles behind Ayushman Bharat, which was initially launched eight years ago. The core idea guiding its inception was to ensure that every Indian citizen could access quality and affordable healthcare services. This vision aimed to alleviate the financial burden associated with medical treatments, making essential healthcare more attainable for millions.</p><p>The scheme’s overarching objective has consistently been to provide robust health coverage and offer financial protection against potentially catastrophic health expenditures. The reported record savings serve as a strong indicator of the program's success in fulfilling its mandate to make healthcare both accessible and financially manageable for a vast segment of the population, thereby contributing to broader public welfare.</p><p>What to watch: The continued expansion and impact of healthcare schemes on public welfare and financial relief.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source, though 'record savings' is an inferential addition not explicitly in the summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/policy/record-savings-on-medical-expenses-under-ayushman-bharat-pm-modi/134427576" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
