     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>SC stays HC order to recover ₹5 lakh from Noida DM in NSA detention case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Supreme Court</span> <span>#High Court</span> <span>#Noida DM</span> <span>#NSA</span></div>
       <p>The Supreme Court has moved to stay a High Court order that mandated the recovery of ₹5 lakh from the District Magistrate (DM) of Noida. This legal action pertains to a case involving a detention under the National Security Act (NSA), and the Supreme Court's decision follows recent submissions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/sc-stays-hc-order-to-recover-5-lakh-from-noida-dm-in-nsa-det.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Senior advocate Mukul Rohatgi, who is representing Medha Roopam, argued before the court that such decisions are not made by a single individual but emerge from a multi-tiered process. He emphasized that, given this collaborative decision-making structure, his client should not be exclusively targeted for a penalty. The argument underscores a contention against singling out an official for financial recovery in complex administrative matters.</p><p>The Supreme Court's stay effectively pauses the High Court's directive for the time being. This action suggests that the apex court will further examine the legal and procedural aspects surrounding the imposition of the penalty. While the specifics of the original NSA detention case remain unelaborated in the immediate context, the focus is now on the challenge to the High Court's recovery order and the broader question of individual accountability in such governmental decisions.</p><p>What to watch: Future Supreme Court hearings will determine the final stance on the High Court's order and its impact on administrative accountability.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithful representation of the source summary and facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/sc-stays-hc-order-to-recover-5-lakh-from-noida-dm-in-nsa-detention-case/article71501204.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/noida/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Noida</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-09-23/sc-stays-hc-order-to-recover-5-lakh-from-noida-dm-in-nsa-det" data-title="SC stays HC order to recover ₹5 lakh from Noida DM in NSA detention case"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
