      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/space">space</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · ScienceDaily Space · 2026-09-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>SpaceX Rocket Impact on Moon Reveals New Crater, NASA Confirms</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#SpaceX</span> <span>#Moon</span> <span>#NASA</span> <span>#Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter</span></div>
       <p>A discarded stage of a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket impacted the Moon on August 5, creating a newly formed crater approximately 60 feet wide, NASA has confirmed. The event, resulting from an uncontrolled descent, has provided scientists with a unique opportunity to study lunar geology.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/spacex-rocket-impact-on-moon-reveals-new-crater-nasa-confirm.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>NASA’s Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter (LRO) was instrumental in capturing detailed images of the impact site. These high-resolution photographs reveal distinct bright and dark streaks of debris that were blasted across the surrounding lunar surface following the collision. The imagery offers crucial insights into the dynamics of such impacts on celestial bodies.</p><p>Significantly, the force of the impact was powerful enough to expose fresh material that had been buried beneath the Moon’s weathered exterior. This exposure of subsurface material is particularly valuable for researchers, as it can provide clues about the Moon's composition and geological history that are otherwise difficult to access.</p><p>The incident, while unintentional, has thus served as an impromptu experiment, allowing scientists to observe the direct consequences of a substantial object striking the lunar surface. The data collected by LRO will contribute to a deeper understanding of crater formation processes and the Moon's stratigraphy.</p><p>What to watch: Further analysis of the exposed lunar material and its implications for lunar composition.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Content aligns with the ScienceDaily source; no fabricated claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/08/260820002429.htm" rel="noopener">ScienceDaily Space</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-09-23/spacex-rocket-impact-on-moon-reveals-new-crater-nasa-confirm" data-title="SpaceX Rocket Impact on Moon Reveals New Crater, NASA Confirms"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
