       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-09-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tehran will not surrender in war with U.S., but believes in diplomacy: Iran President tells UN</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Iran</span> <span>#United States</span> <span>#UN</span> <span>#diplomacy</span></div>
       <p>During an address to the United Nations, Iran's President Masoud Pezeshkian conveyed a dual message regarding the nation's stance in potential conflict with the United States, asserting that Tehran would not surrender but also expressing belief in diplomacy. The speech was marked by symbolic gestures and a notable walkout from the U.S. delegation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/tehran-will-not-surrender-in-war-with-us-but-believes-in-dip.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>President Pezeshkian held up photographs during his address. These images included a picture of the late Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei. Additionally, he displayed photos of more than 150 school children, reportedly killed during the initial days of a conflict, though the specific conflict was not detailed in the summary.</p><p>In a diplomatic incident, the United States delegation chose to walk out of the assembly at the very beginning of President Pezeshkian's speech. This early departure signaled a clear protest or disagreement with the Iranian leader's presence or anticipated remarks.</p><p>The Iranian President's statement to the UN underscores the complex and often tense relationship between Iran and the United States. While emphasizing a firm national resolve against surrender, the inclusion of a belief in diplomacy suggests an open, albeit cautious, avenue for engagement. The dramatic visual aids and the U.S. walkout further highlighted the deep divisions and high stakes in international relations concerning Iran.</p><p>What to watch: Diplomatic engagements between Iran and the U.S. following the UN address.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithfully reflects the events described in the summary regarding President Pezeshkian's UN speech and the US walkout.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-president-masoud-pezeshkian-un-general-assembly-wartime-speech-us-israel/article71500620.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
