       <h1>Zaheer Khan Replaces Stephen Fleming as CSK Coach Ahead of IPL 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#IPL</span> <span>#CSK</span> <span>#Coaching</span></div>
       <p>The Chennai Super Kings (CSK) have announced a significant change in their coaching staff ahead of the Indian Premier League (IPL) 2027 season. Zaheer Khan has officially taken over as the head coach, replacing long-serving mentor Stephen Fleming.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-23/zaheer-khan-replaces-stephen-fleming-as-csk-coach-ahead-of-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Fleming's departure marks the end of an era for the Chennai franchise. He had been at the helm for an impressive 18 seasons, during which he played an instrumental role in shaping CSK into one of the most successful teams in the world's biggest T20 league. Under his guidance, CSK achieved remarkable consistency and secured multiple titles, establishing a formidable legacy in the tournament.</p><p>Zaheer Khan, a prominent figure in Indian cricket, now steps into a pivotal role, tasked with continuing the team's tradition of excellence. This transition signals a new chapter for the Super Kings as they prepare for the challenges of the upcoming IPL season. The change in leadership at such a crucial position will undoubtedly draw considerable attention from fans and analysts alike, eager to see the direction the team takes under its new coach.</p><p>What to watch: The strategic direction and team performance under Zaheer Khan's new leadership in IPL 2027.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithfully reflects the source summary regarding Zaheer Khan replacing Stephen Fleming for CSK ahead of IPL 2027.</p>
